  "checks": [
    "both contrib layouts compile from an explicit public application bundle, packaged Tendriller runtime and pinned WASM assets",
    "the built scope recipe rejects a durably queued stale edit after reset and preserves the original accepted retry without another write",
    "independent browser identities and OPFS replicas render one shared team-owned task through the actual selected Tendriller backend",
    "typing traverses authenticated ephemeral frames, expires and leaves no durable event",
    "with the finality clock held through inclusion, disconnected competing claims resolve by deterministic author order to one acceptance and one SQL rejection",
    "a failed SQL guard emits no intent; the final winning intent runs the native worker once and records a correlated result that browser scope cannot forge",
    "a delayed durable append reply preserves newer typing and cannot regress the already observed final receipt",
    "Worker termination before reply delivery reopens durable identity and original operation; one message survives with its saved draft and original proposal ID",
    "both layouts rebuild from retained final events without redispatching the worker or writing host application state",
    "independent replicas receive identical task/chat final events over WebRTC after every host introduction socket has closed",
    "warm authenticated WebRTC sessions finalize new chat while the host listener is stopped, with increasing RTC bytes and exactly zero host requests or signaling growth",
    "fresh RTC introduction recovers the same signed history and exact outcomes after interruption, including four 192 KiB programs of sixteen 12 KiB events, with measured bytes and bounded queues"
